 ## Overview
-Multiresolution Volume Rendering is a direct volume ray casting technique that exploits hierarchical data structures (such as wavelet or Laplacian pyramids) to perform adaptive integration and early termination [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of high computational cost in standard ray casting by allowing the use of lower-resolution data for parts of the ray where accuracy requirements are lower or occlusion is high, thereby reducing the number of voxels computed and increasing step lengths [S1, unofficial].
